  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "• Boil the kettle. Half-fill a medium saucepan with boiling water.\n• Add basmati rice, currants and a pinch of salt and cook, uncovered, over high heat until tender, 12 minutes. Drain.\n• Return to saucepan. Add the butter and baby spinach leaves and stir to melt and combine. Season to taste. Cover to keep warm.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/63688502272a7705f90f54d2/step-a7e61e63.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Meanwhile, cut or tear each spinach falafel into quarters (don't worry if they crumble!).\n• Roughly chop tomato, cucumber and mint.\n• In a medium bowl, combine tomatoes, cucumber, mint and a drizzle of white wine vinegar and olive oil. Season with a pinch of salt and pepper.\n• In a small bowl, combine dill & parsley mayonnaise, Greek-style yoghurt and a splash of water. Season to taste.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/63688502272a7705f90f54d2/step-4aa1bdb8.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Heat a large frying pan over medium-high heat and add olive oil (1/4 cup for 2 people / 1/2 cup for 4 people).\n• When oil is hot, cook falafels, tossing, until deep golden brown, 4-6 minutes.\n• In last minute of cook time, add garlic & herb seasoning and sesame seeds and toss to combine.\n• Transfer to a paper towel lined plate.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/63688502272a7705f90f54d2/step-cf093aff.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Divide currant-butter rice between bowls.\n• Top with sesame falafel, tomato mint salsa and herby sauce to serve. Enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/63688502272a7705f90f54d2/step-bb460d2f.jpg"
    }
  ]
